14:T4a9,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"International Prayer Timetables: Bangladesh (Dhaka) and UAE (Dubai, Sharjah, Ajman) Waqt Guidelines and Eid Timings","description":"Complete prayer schedules for Dhaka (Bangladesh) and UAE (Dubai, Sharjah, Ajman). Includes Fajr last time Dhaka, Sehri boundaries, and Eid namaz timing.","image":["https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512453979798-5ea266f8880c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80"],"datePublished":"2026-10-11T12:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-10-11T12:00:00Z","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Sheikh Dr. Aminul Islam & Global Editorial Team","url":"https://namazeshariq.com/about"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Namaz-e-Shariq","url":"https://namazeshariq.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://namazeshariq.com/web-app-manifest-512x512.png"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://namazeshariq.com/blog/international-prayer-timetables-dhaka-dubai-sharjah-ajman"},"keywords":"namaz time dhaka, namaz time today dhaka, fajr namaz last time dhaka, bangladesh namaz time, namaz timing sharjah, namaz time in sharjah, namaz timing in sharjah, eid namaz time dubai, namaz time ajman"}15:T664,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the \"Fajr namaz last time\" in Dhaka?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The last time to pray Fajr in Dhaka is immediately before the upper edge of the sun breaches the eastern horizon (Sunrise / Shurooq). Once sunrise begins, Fajr time has expired, and praying at that exact moment is prohibited until the sun has risen a spear’s length (approx. 15-20 minutes after sunrise)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What calculation standard is utilized in the United Arab Emirates?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The General Authority of Islamic Affairs and Endowments (Awqaf) and the Dubai Islamic Affairs and Charitable Activities Department (IACAD) publish unified, official timetables based on the Umm Al-Qura twilight standard (18.5° for Fajr, and Maghrib plus 90 minutes for Isha)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is Eid namaz time determined in Dubai and Sharjah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Eid prayer in the UAE is scheduled approximately 15 to 20 minutes after sunrise on the 1st of Shawwal (Eid ul-Fitr) and 10th of Dhul Hijjah (Eid ul-Adha). The exact minute is announced across official UAE government media."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the divisional prayer time differences across Bangladesh?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Compared to the Dhaka baseline, eastern divisions like Sylhet and Chittagong experience sunrise and sunset 4 to 6 minutes earlier, while western divisions like Rajshahi, Rangpur, and Khulna experience them 5 to 7 minutes later."}}]}a:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950 min-h-screen py-10 transition-colors duration-200","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$14"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://namazeshariq.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Articles\",\"item\":\"https://namazeshariq.com/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"International Prayer Timetables: Bangladesh (Dhaka) and UAE (Dubai, Sharjah, Ajman) Waqt Guidelines and Eid Timings\",\"item\":\"https://namazeshariq.com/blog/international-prayer-timetables-dhaka-dubai-sharjah-ajman\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$15"}}],"$L16"]}]
