21:["$","$L26",null,{"items":[{"question":"What is the \"Fajr namaz last time\" in Dhaka?","answer":"The last time to pray Fajr in Dhaka is immediately before the upper edge of the sun breaches the eastern horizon (Sunrise / Shurooq). Once sunrise begins, Fajr time has expired, and praying at that exact moment is prohibited until the sun has risen a spear’s length (approx. 15-20 minutes after sunrise)."},{"question":"What calculation standard is utilized in the United Arab Emirates?","answer":"The General Authority of Islamic Affairs and Endowments (Awqaf) and the Dubai Islamic Affairs and Charitable Activities Department (IACAD) publish unified, official timetables based on the Umm Al-Qura twilight standard (18.5° for Fajr, and Maghrib plus 90 minutes for Isha)."},{"question":"How is Eid namaz time determined in Dubai and Sharjah?","answer":"Eid prayer in the UAE is scheduled approximately 15 to 20 minutes after sunrise on the 1st of Shawwal (Eid ul-Fitr) and 10th of Dhul Hijjah (Eid ul-Adha). The exact minute is announced across official UAE government media."},{"question":"What are the divisional prayer time differences across Bangladesh?","answer":"Compared to the Dhaka baseline, eastern divisions like Sylhet and Chittagong experience sunrise and sunset 4 to 6 minutes earlier, while western divisions like Rajshahi, Rangpur, and Khulna experience them 5 to 7 minutes later."}],"title":"Key Questions & Rulings Answered"}]
